/target
**/node_modules
.next/
storybook-static/
dist/
*.log
# `next build` turns on `incremental`, which drops a tsbuildinfo next to the app.
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
cypress/screenshots/
cypress/videos/

# Throwaway secrets, and the generated config that names their public halves,
# for the compose e2e and demo stacks:
#   just gen-e2e-signing-key  -> .e2e/oauth-signing-key.pem      (the OP's key)
#   just gen-demo-keys        -> .e2e/demo-merchant/…            (the merchant's)
#                                .e2e/application-demo.yml       (its public JWK)
# The whole directory is ignored deliberately, including the YAML: it is
# generated per checkout from a key that exists nowhere else, so a committed
# copy would register a merchant nobody can authenticate as.
.e2e/
